    "created_at": "2025-01-21T10:25:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-01-21T10:25:36Z",
    "body": "The first issue will be fixed by PR #312. We plan to release sQUlearn 0.8.1 today or tomorrow, which will resolve the issue.\n\nThe error  `RuntimeError: Failed to execute job on simulator!`  is thrown by Qiskit, not by sQUlearn.\n\nI suspect IBM has shut down all simulators in their cloud. At least,  `backend = service.backends(simulator=True)`  \nreturns an empty list for me. Maybe, you may have some special access.\n\nRegarding the failure  `RuntimeError: Failed to execute job on simulator!`,  I believe the issue is that your data is not within the boundaries of (-1, 1) for the Chebyshev encoding. This encoding uses `Ry(arccos(x))`, and `arccos(x)` is only well-defined for values of `x` within (-1, 1).\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
